# .check-links-ignore — paths exempt from bin/check-links
#
# These are live-but-historical, generated, or reasoning-trail files whose
# links are NOT a navigation contract, so a stale link in them is expected and
# not a defect. One gitignore-style glob (or path prefix) per line; blank lines
# and `#` comments ignored.
#
# General categories — dot-dirs (.integrated/ .archived/ .routing-trail/ …),
# `_obs/`, `_archive/`, `ref/converted/`, and component `…-core/src/` segment
# links (lint-outline's domain) — are excluded in bin/check-links itself. This
# file is for the repo-specific rest. Keep it honest: exempt only files whose
# links are genuinely point-in-time, not files you'd rather not fix.

